IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cra-cremation`

-- Cremation Act 1929 (WA), arranging a cremation -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_cremation-act-1929_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Life facts are from the workbench scenario au/wa/cradle-to-grave-chloe/facts.json: c086 (2052-08-19, a Monday) Graham
-- dies at 82 at home; the funeral director registers the death; a cremation permit; not a reportable death; his will
-- (c087) makes Chloe executor and leaves everything to Sue, his widow. c098 (2088-11-02) Chloe dies at 85; her will to the
-- children equally; Oliver executor. That each death was from natural causes certified by the deceased's own GP, that the
-- funeral director applies on Chloe's written authority, and that Ella wants the ashes, are ASSUMED for the cases; the
-- scenario does not say. Variants change one fact each.

