§ `s 2 -- am I an administrator`

-- c086: Chloe, the executor, is an administrator.
#ASSERT `Am I an administrator` `Chloe, Graham's executor`
-- s 2: lawful custody of the body is enough -- the funeral director holding it is an administrator.
#ASSERT `Am I an administrator` `the funeral director, holding Graham's body`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I an administrator` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority`
-- c086: Sue is not the executor, and with an executor named she is not asked to have the best right to administration.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I an administrator` `Sue, Graham's widow, not his executor`

§ `s 8(3A), s 13(1) -- may I apply`

-- c086: Chloe applies as executor.
#ASSERT `May I apply for the permit` `Chloe, Graham's executor` `c086: Graham at 82, at home, natural causes, his GP certified`
-- c086: the funeral director applies on Chloe's written authority (s 8(3A)(b)).
#ASSERT `May I apply for the permit` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority` `c086: Graham at 82, at home, natural causes, his GP certified`
-- Being the widow is not enough on its own.
#ASSERT NOT `May I apply for the permit` `Sue, Graham's widow, not his executor` `c086: Graham at 82, at home, natural causes, his GP certified`
#ASSERT `May I apply for the permit` `Sue, Graham's widow, satisfying the referee` `c086: Graham at 82, at home, natural causes, his GP certified`
#ASSERT NOT `May I apply for the permit` `Chloe, Graham's executor, knowing Sue has objected in writing` `c086 variant: Sue has objected in writing`
#ASSERT `May I apply for the permit` `Chloe, Graham's executor, knowing Sue has objected in writing` `c086 variant: Sue has objected in writing; Graham's attested will asks for cremation`

§ `s 8(3B) -- the statutory declaration`

#ASSERT NOT `Must I make a statutory declaration` `Chloe, Graham's executor`
-- Acting on the executor's authority does not make the funeral director an administrator.
#ASSERT `Must I make a statutory declaration` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority`
#ASSERT NOT `Must I make a statutory declaration` `the funeral director, holding Graham's body`

§ `s 8(4A), Regulations Sch 2 item 3 -- the fee`

-- c086: the permit given on Monday 19 August 2052 at 10 am.
#ASSERT `What fee must I pay for the permit` `Monday to Friday` 10 EQUALS 89.10
-- 5 pm is outside ordinary hours on the reading taken.
#ASSERT `What fee must I pay for the permit` `Monday to Friday` 17 EQUALS 147.40
#ASSERT `What fee must I pay for the permit` `Saturday` 11.5 EQUALS 89.10
#ASSERT `What fee must I pay for the permit` `Saturday` 13 EQUALS 147.40
#ASSERT `What fee must I pay for the permit` `public holiday` 10 EQUALS 147.40

§ `s 8A(g), s 12 -- the certifying doctor`

-- c086
#ASSERT `Can the doctor's certificate support the permit` `Graham's GP, unrelated`
#ASSERT NOT `Can the doctor's certificate support the permit` `a doctor who is the deceased's nephew`
-- s 8A(g) does not list a spouse.
#ASSERT `Can the doctor's certificate support the permit` `a doctor married to the deceased, taking nothing on the death`
-- s 12: but a spouse who takes property on the death may not certify.
#ASSERT NOT `Can the doctor's certificate support the permit` `a doctor married to the deceased, who inherits`
#ASSERT NOT `Can the doctor's certificate support the permit` `a doctor in partnership with the medical referee`

§ `s 8A(b), s 13 -- the deceased's wishes and the family's objection`

#ASSERT NOT `Does the deceased's direction stop the cremation` `c086: Graham at 82, at home, natural causes, his GP certified`
#ASSERT `Does the deceased's direction stop the cremation` `c086 variant: Graham left a written direction not to be cremated`
#ASSERT NOT `Does the deceased's direction stop the cremation` `c086 variant: Graham's written direction against, the Chief Health Officer orders cremation`
#ASSERT NOT `Does the family's objection stop the cremation` `c086: Graham at 82, at home, natural causes, his GP certified`
#ASSERT `Does the family's objection stop the cremation` `c086 variant: Sue has objected in writing`
#ASSERT NOT `Does the family's objection stop the cremation` `c086 variant: Sue has objected in writing; Graham's attested will asks for cremation`
-- c098: Oliver, as executor, must use all reasonable endeavours.
#ASSERT `Must I try to carry out the deceased's wish to be cremated` `Oliver, Chloe's executor` `c098 variant: Chloe's attested will asks for cremation`
#ASSERT NOT `Must I try to carry out the deceased's wish to be cremated` `Ella, Chloe's daughter, not her executor` `c098 variant: Chloe's attested will asks for cremation`

§ `ss 8, 8A -- what the medical referee will do`

-- c086: Graham's natural death at home, certified by his GP; the referee must grant the permit.
#ASSERT `What will the referee do with my application` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority` `c086: Graham at 82, at home, natural causes, his GP certified` TRUE EQUALS `grant the permit, as s 8(2) requires`
-- Without Form 6, the fee and a Form 7 or coroner's certificate (r 11, 12).
#ASSERT `What will the referee do with my application` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority` `c086: Graham at 82, at home, natural causes, his GP certified` FALSE EQUALS `refuse it; I may ask the State Administrative Tribunal to review the refusal (s 8(6))`
#ASSERT `What will the referee do with my application` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority` `c086 variant: the death appears suspicious to the referee` TRUE EQUALS `refuse it and report the death to the coroner (s 8(5)); a permit only on a coroner's certificate`
#ASSERT `What will the referee do with my application` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority` `c086 variant: appears suspicious, a coroner has certified the permit may be granted` TRUE EQUALS `grant the permit, as s 8(2) requires`
#ASSERT `What will the referee do with my application` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority` `c086 variant: the coroner will investigate` TRUE EQUALS `refuse it until the coroner certifies that it may be granted (s 8A(f))`
#ASSERT `What will the referee do with my application` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority` `c086 variant: certified by Graham's nephew` TRUE EQUALS `refuse it; I may ask the State Administrative Tribunal to review the refusal (s 8(6))`
#ASSERT `What will the referee do with my application` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority` `c086 variant: Graham left a written direction not to be cremated` TRUE EQUALS `refuse it; I may ask the State Administrative Tribunal to review the refusal (s 8(6))`
#ASSERT `What will the referee do with my application` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority` `c086 variant: Sue has objected in writing` TRUE EQUALS `refuse it; I may ask the State Administrative Tribunal to review the refusal (s 8(6))`
-- s 8A(a) has no coronial exception: on the text a coroner's certificate does not replace the s 44 certificate.
#ASSERT `What will the referee do with my application` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority` `c086 variant: no s 44 certificate, a coroner has certified the permit may be granted` TRUE EQUALS `refuse it; I may ask the State Administrative Tribunal to review the refusal (s 8(6))`
-- A s 14 order binds the cremation, not the grant of the permit.
#ASSERT `What will the referee do with my application` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority` `c086 variant: a coroner forbids cremation absolutely` TRUE EQUALS `grant the permit, as s 8(2) requires`
-- c098: Oliver applies as Chloe's executor.
#ASSERT `Will I be granted the permit` `Oliver, Chloe's executor` `c098: Chloe at 85, natural causes, her GP certified` TRUE
-- c098: Ella, not the executor and without his authority, may not.
#ASSERT NOT `Will I be granted the permit` `Ella, Chloe's daughter, not her executor` `c098: Chloe at 85, natural causes, her GP certified` TRUE

§ `s 8(5), s 8A(f), s 14 -- the coroner`

-- c086: not a reportable death, nothing suspicious.
#ASSERT NOT `Must the coroner be involved` `c086: Graham at 82, at home, natural causes, his GP certified`
#ASSERT `Must the coroner be involved` `c086 variant: the death appears suspicious to the referee`
#ASSERT `Must the coroner be involved` `c086 variant: a coroner forbids cremation absolutely`
#ASSERT `May I ask the Tribunal to review the refusal` FALSE
-- A refusal under s 8(5) goes to the coroner, not the Tribunal.
#ASSERT NOT `May I ask the Tribunal to review the refusal` TRUE

§ `ss 3, 9, 10, 13, 14; Form 9 -- may the cremation go ahead`

-- c086: permit granted, two days after the death, at a licensed crematorium.
#ASSERT `May the cremation go ahead now` `c086: Graham at 82, at home, natural causes, his GP certified` TRUE 48 TRUE
-- Form 9: the permit is not valid until 24 hours after death.
#ASSERT NOT `May the cremation go ahead now` `c086: Graham at 82, at home, natural causes, his GP certified` TRUE 20 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May the cremation go ahead now` `c086: Graham at 82, at home, natural causes, his GP certified` TRUE 48 FALSE
#ASSERT `May the cremation go ahead now` `c086 variant: forbidden until organs removed; they have been` TRUE 48 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May the cremation go ahead now` `c086 variant: forbidden until organs removed; not yet` TRUE 48 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May the cremation go ahead now` `c086 variant: a coroner forbids cremation absolutely` TRUE 48 TRUE

§ `s 7 -- the ashes`

-- c098: Oliver obtained the permit, so the ashes may be delivered to him.
#ASSERT `May the ashes be delivered to me` TRUE
-- c098: Ella did not obtain the permit; the crematorium may not deliver them to her.
#ASSERT NOT `May the ashes be delivered to me` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `May the ashes be removed` FALSE FALSE

§ `s 13(1), s 15 -- offences`

#ASSERT `Would applying be an offence` `Chloe, Graham's executor, knowing Sue has objected in writing` `c086 variant: Sue has objected in writing`
#ASSERT NOT `Would applying be an offence` `Chloe, Graham's executor, knowing Sue has objected in writing` `c086 variant: Sue has objected in writing; Graham's attested will asks for cremation`
#ASSERT NOT `Would applying be an offence` `Chloe, Graham's executor` `c086: Graham at 82, at home, natural causes, his GP certified`
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be imprisoned in months` EQUALS 12
